=== vector width: full occupancy vs starved =================
  vw=1   full-occupancy 0.350 ms (766.5 GB/s)   starved 0.392 ms (684.5 GB/s)
  vw=2   full-occupancy 0.341 ms (787.3 GB/s)   starved 0.347 ms (773.3 GB/s)
  vw=4   full-occupancy 0.333 ms (806.6 GB/s)   starved 0.345 ms (777.9 GB/s)
  PREDICTION: full-occupancy row is flat across widths (issue is ~138x
  from being the limiter); starved row shows a large win, because vector
  width buys memory-level parallelism and MLP is only scarce when
  occupancy is scarce. If BOTH are flat, the starvation was insufficient.

